## 📊 3.2 Hierarchical Logging Integration (MANDATORY)

### **Requirements by Layer**

**Test Scenario Layer**:
- **(MANDATORY)** Import `TestLogger` from `Engine/Shared/TestLogger`
- **(MANDATORY)** Call `TestLogger.reset()` at test start
- **(MANDATORY)** Wrap all test steps with `TestLogger.testStep()`
- **(MANDATORY)** Use human-readable descriptions (e.g., `'Login to application'`)
- **(MANDATORY)** NO `console.log` - use `TestLogger.info()`, `TestLogger.warn()`, `TestLogger.error()`

**Business Workflow Layer**:
- **(MANDATORY)** Import `TestLogger` from `Engine/Shared/TestLogger`
- **(MANDATORY)** Wrap all business methods with `TestLogger.businessStep()`
- **(MANDATORY)** Include relevant business context (username, item name, etc.)
- **(MANDATORY)** NO technical details (locators, element IDs)

**Page Objects Layer**:
- **(MANDATORY)** Import `TestLogger` from `Engine/Shared/TestLogger`
- **(MANDATORY)** Wrap all page methods with `TestLogger.pageStep()`
- **(MANDATORY)** Describe WHAT is being done, not technical HOW
- **(MANDATORY)** NO locators or CSS selectors in descriptions

**Pattern Example**:
```typescript
import { TestLogger } from 'Engine/Shared/TestLogger';

// Test Scenario
test('User login', async ({ page }) => {
  TestLogger.reset();
  
  await TestLogger.testStep('Login to application', async () => {
    await loginWorkflow.performLogin(baseUrl, username, password);
  });
});

// Business Workflow
async performLogin(baseUrl: string, username: string, password: string): Promise<void> {
  await TestLogger.businessStep(`Login with username: ${username}`, async () => {
    await this.loginPage.navigateToLogin(baseUrl);
    await this.loginPage.login(username, password);
  });
}

// Page Object
async login(username: string, password: string): Promise<void> {
  await TestLogger.pageStep('Fill login credentials and submit', async () => {
    await this.usernameInput.fill(username);
    await this.passwordInput.fill(password);
    await this.loginButton.click();
  });
}
```

